# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository regardless of the
# checking-out platform's autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true silently rewrites tracked text files
# to CRLF, which then disagrees with Prettier's default `lf` output
# (format:check fails on files nobody actually edited) and, worse,
# breaks a Git hook's shebang line outright (`#!/usr/bin/env node\r`
# resolves to a nonexistent interpreter named "node\r"). See
# .project/decisions/ADR-009-git-hook-enforcement-mechanism.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Hook scripts specifically: exec'd directly via shebang, so this is a
# functional requirement here, not just a formatting preference.
tooling/git-hooks/* text eol=lf
